194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434996 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434986 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434996 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434989 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434996 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434990 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434996 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434992 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434996 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434996 1077 "selection" 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434996 1078 #edb/ref 17592186434989 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434996 1079 #uuid "d03d6b86-3f28-58b0-a2eb-4595cf7f0086" 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434997 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434996 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434997 1069 "q-163049" 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434997 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434997 1071 "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=xy-{y}^{3},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434997 1072 #uuid "ce8393ed-c395-5936-8ac5-87c9fbd01992" 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434997 1074 "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy-{y}^{3})=y, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy-{y}^{3})=x-3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}y & x-3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand ${f}^{′}$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}(-1) & (2)-3(-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434998 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434995 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434998 1069 "q-163077" 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434998 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434998 1071 "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1),\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-∗=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434998 1072 #uuid "df9f8fb7-c1aa-51d4-afc9-10cbbb747f39" 13194139534749 17592186045417 true] [17592186434998 1074 "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1)=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1},\\, & \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1)=\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1} & \\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡6,\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe tangent to $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-f(a)={f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nz-\\operatorname{ln}⁡6=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡6+(-\\frac{1}{3})+\\frac{2}{3}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡6+\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" 13194139534749 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-1424145b-0da3-5017-9706-c1a6388f4d65" 17592186434985 "answer-16a4098a-0497-5a4a-9073-508d8b62e0f0" 17592186434986 "answer-7054d950-8f37-587d-a33e-968d65e47cb7" 17592186434987 "answer-